'''Esteban José Jean-Pierre Ocon-Khelfane''' ({{IPA|fr|ɛs.te.ban ɔ.kɔ̃}}; born 17 September 1996) is a French [[racing driver]] who competes in [[Formula One]] for [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]]. Ocon won the [[2021 Hungarian Grand Prix]] with [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]].

Born and raised in [[Normandy]] to a [[working-class]] family, Ocon began competitive [[kart racing]] aged nine, winning several national and international titles. Graduating to [[junior formulae]] in 2012, Ocon won his first title at the [[2014 FIA Formula 3 European Championship]] with [[Prema Racing|Prema]], ahead of [[Tom Blomqvist]] and [[Max Verstappen]]. Ocon then won the [[2015 GP3 Series]] with [[ART Grand Prix|ART]], achieving 14 podiums in 18 races. A member of the [[Mercedes Junior Team]] since 2015, Ocon made his Formula One debut at the [[2016 Belgian Grand Prix]] with [[Manor Racing|Manor]], replacing [[Rio Haryanto]]  for the remainder of the {{F1|2016}} season. He moved to [[Force India]]—who later became [[Racing Point Force India|Racing Point]]—in {{F1|2017}}, partnering [[Sergio Pérez]]. Ocon left Racing Point at the end of {{F1|2018}}, becoming a reserve driver for [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]] in {{F1|2019}}.

Ocon returned as a full-time driver with [[Renault in Formula One|Renault]] in {{F1|2020}}, taking his maiden podium finish at the {{F1GP|2020|Sakhir}}. Retaining his seat for {{F1|2021}}, Ocon partnered [[Fernando Alonso]] at the re-branded [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]], taking his maiden [[List of Formula One Grand Prix winners|victory]] at the [[2021 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungarian Grand Prix]]. After a less successful {{F1|2022}} campaign, during which he became the first teammate to outscore Alonso in the championship since [[Jenson Button]] in {{F1|2015}}, Ocon achieved his third podium at the [[2023 Monaco Grand Prix]]. In {{F1|2024}}—his final season at Alpine—Ocon achieved his maiden [[List of Formula One drivers who set a fastest lap|fastest lap]] in the [[2024 United States Grand Prix|United States]], followed by a fourth career podium at the rain-affected {{F1GP|2024|São Paulo}}. He left Alpine after the {{F1GP|2024|Qatar}}, moving to [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] for {{F1|2025}} alongside [[Oliver Bearman]].

As of the {{Latest F1GP}}, Ocon has achieved {{Numbertoword|{{F1stat|OCO|wins}}}} race win, {{Numbertoword|{{F1stat|OCO|fastestlaps}}}} fastest lap and {{Numbertoword|{{F1stat|OCO|podiums}}}} podiums in Formula One. Ocon is contracted to remain at Haas until at least the end of the 2026 season.

== Early and personal life ==
Esteban José Jean-Pierre Ocon-Khelfane was born on 17 September 1996 in [[Évreux]], [[Normandy]] to Sabrina Khelfane and Laurent Ocon, a mechanic who owns a garage in Évreux.<ref name="FN">{{cite web |author1=Petr Kubala |title=Carl, José, Maria, Joseph. Znáte celá jména jezdců formule 1? |url=https://f1sport.auto.cz/clanek/cela-jmena-jezdcu-f1#part=3 |website=F1sport.cz |access-date=25 April 2021 |language=cs |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425123122/https://f1sport.auto.cz/clanek/cela-jmena-jezdcu-f1#part=3 |url-status=live }}</ref> His paternal family is originally from [[Málaga]], Spain, and his mother has roots in Algeria.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://lemag.seinesaintdenis.fr/Esteban-Ocon-la-vie-en-pole|title=Esteban Ocon, la vie en pole|website=Seine-Saint-Denis – Le magazine|access-date=27 April 2017|archive-date=28 April 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170428054232/http://lemag.seinesaintdenis.fr/Esteban-Ocon-la-vie-en-pole|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.planetf1.com/driver/esteban-ocon/biography|title=Esteban Ocon Biography|website=PlanetF1}}</ref> While competing in karting, his parents decided to sell their family home, which included his father's garage, to fund his karting career. After selling the house, they lived and travelled to races in a caravan Ocon also used as a motor home.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Richards|first=Giles|date=27 August 2021|title=Esteban Ocon: I didn't have the right to fail, I had to succeed|url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/aug/27/esteban-ocon-formula-one-i-didnt-have-the-right-to-fail-i-had-to-succeed|url-status=live|access-date=22 October 2021|website=[[The Guardian]]|archive-date=22 October 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211022204814/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/aug/27/esteban-ocon-formula-one-i-didnt-have-the-right-to-fail-i-had-to-succeed}}</ref> Ocon admitted that he almost gave up on his racing career to work at [[McDonald's]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.thetimes.com/article/i-nearly-went-to-work-in-mcdonalds-admits-f1s-rising-star-esteban-ocon-3vl652w0f |title=I nearly went to work in McDonald's, admits F1's rising star Esteban Ocon |first=Rebecca |last=Clancy |date=15 July 2017 |access-date=12 December 2024 |work=[[The Times]] |publisher=[[News UK]] |issn=0140-0460}}</ref>

{{As of|2022}}, Ocon lives in [[Geneva]], Switzerland. Besides his native French language, Ocon also speaks English, Spanish and Italian. In 2023 Ocon began a relationship with  model, social media influencer, medical student and former [[Miss Côte d'Azur]] Flavy Barla having split with his previous girlfriend Elena Berri (whom he had started dating in 2018) earlier in 2023.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.essentiallysports.com/f1-news-alpine-news-who-is-flavy-barla-esteban-ocons-new-girlfriend-after-his-breakup-with-elena-berri/ | title=Who is Flavy Barla? – Esteban Ocon's New Girlfriend After His Breakup with Elena Berri | date=30 December 2023 }}</ref>

== Junior racing career ==
=== Karting (2006–2011) ===
Ocon entered [[karting]] in 2006, when he finished eighth in the Minime class of the French Championship.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.driverdb.com/standings/1247-2006/|title=Championnat de France&nbsp;– Minime 2006|work=driverdb.com|publisher=Driver Database|access-date=18 October 2013|archive-date=19 October 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131019170635/http://www.driverdb.com/standings/1247-2006/|url-status=live}}</ref> He won the championship in 2007 and continued his success by winning the Cadet class in 2008 ahead of [[Anthoine Hubert]] and [[Pierre Gasly]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.driverdb.com/standings/1247-2007/|title=Championnat de France&nbsp;– Minime 2007|work=driverdb.com|publisher=Driver Database|access-date=18 October 2013|archive-date=19 October 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131019170631/http://www.driverdb.com/standings/1247-2007/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.driverdb.com/standings/2456-2008/|title=Championnat de France&nbsp;– Cadet 2008|work=driverdb.com|publisher=Driver Database|access-date=18 October 2013|archive-date=19 October 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131019170628/http://www.driverdb.com/standings/2456-2008/|url-status=live}}</ref> He then spent three years racing in the [[KF3]] category and competed in the [[Spanish Karting Championship|Spanish Championship]] and [[Italian Open Masters]]. He won the French KF3 title in 2010 and finished as runner-up in the [[WSK Euro Series]] in 2011 behind [[Max Verstappen]].<ref name="One">{{cite news|url=http://www.paddockscout.com/lotuss-one-to-watch-esteban-ocon/|title=Lotus's one to watch: Esteban Ocon|last=Musker|first=Ant|date=4 October 2013|publisher=Paddock Scout|access-date=18 October 2013|archive-date=20 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201020064837/https://www.paddockscout.com/lotuss-one-to-watch-esteban-ocon|url-status=live}}</ref> At the age of 14, Ocon was signed by Gravity Sports management, a sister company of [[Renault in Formula One|Renault F1]] team.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/february-2015/93/esteban-ocon|title=Esteban Ocon|date=9 July 2015|work=Motor Sport Magazine|access-date=27 April 2017|language=en|archive-date=28 April 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170428053018/http://www.motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/february-2015/93/esteban-ocon|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Formula Renault 2.0 (2012–2013) ===
==== 2012: Junior formulae debut ====
In 2012, Ocon made his debut in [[Open-wheel car|single-seaters]], taking part in the [[2012 Eurocup Formula Renault 2.0|Eurocup Formula Renault 2.0]] with [[Koiranen GP|Koiranen Motorsport]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.italiaracing.net/notizia.asp?id=34122&cat=22|title=Ocon e Pakari pronti per il debutto|date=13 December 2011|trans-title=Ocon and Pacari ready for debut|work=ItaliaRacing.net|publisher=Inpagina|language=it|access-date=13 December 2011|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120601115038/http://www.italiaracing.net/notizia.asp?id=34122&cat=22|archive-date=1 June 2012}}</ref> He finished fourteenth with four point-scoring finishes, including being on the podium at his home round at [[Circuit Paul Ricard]].<ref name="One"/> He also contested a partial campaign in the [[2012 Formula Renault 2.0 Alps Series|Formula Renault 2.0 Alps]] with Koiranen,<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.renaultsportitalia.it/art/news_20120131_alps_eng.html|title=F.Renault 2.0 ALPS synonimous (sic) of quality with top team and drivers ready to roll in 2012 season|date=8 March 2012|work=Renaultsport Italia|publisher=Fast Lane Promotion|access-date=8 March 2012|archive-date=28 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201128024024/http://www.renaultsportitalia.it/art/news_20120131_alps_eng.html|url-status=live}}</ref> finishing seventh with two podiums, both of which came at the [[Red Bull Ring]].

==== 2013: Maiden victories in the Eurocup and Northern European Cup ====
Ocon remained in the series for [[2013 Eurocup Formula Renault 2.0|2013]], switching to the [[R-ace GP|ART Junior Team]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.gpupdate.net/en/f1-news/290630/lotus-f1-junior-team-drivers-announced/|title=Lotus F1 Junior Team drivers announced|date=15 February 2013|work=GPUpdate.net|publisher=JHED Media BV|access-date=15 February 2013|archive-date=1 December 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201131748/https://www.gpupdate.net/en/f1-news/290630/lotus-f1-junior-team-drivers-announced/|url-status=live}}</ref> He recorded one [[pole position]] and won two races including at Circuit Paul Ricard, finishing the season in third place behind Pierre Gasly and [[Oliver Rowland]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.paddockscout.com/ocon-takes-first-eurocup-victory-in-frantic-race-two/|title=Ocon takes first Eurocup victory in frantic race two|last=Musker|first=Ant|date=29 September 2013|publisher=Paddock Scout|access-date=18 October 2013|archive-date=20 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201020064825/https://www.paddockscout.com/ocon-takes-first-eurocup-victory-in-frantic-race-two|url-status=live}}</ref> A partial campaign in the [[2013 Formula Renault 2.0 Northern European Cup|Northern European Cup]] produced a race win at the [[Hockenheimring]] and two further podiums.

=== Formula Three (2013–2014) ===
==== 2013: F3 debut at Macau ====
[[File:2014 F3 HockenheimringII Esteban Ocon by 2eight 8SC1548.jpg|thumb|Esteban Ocon in F3 – Hockenheimring 2014]]
Ocon made his debut in [[Formula Three]] machinery at the [[2013 Macau Grand Prix]] with [[Prema Powerteam]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/110665|title=Lotus Formula 1 protege Esteban Ocon gets Prema Macau Formula 3 seat|last=Simmons|first=Marcus|date=15 October 2013|work=[[Autosport]]|publisher=[[Haymarket Media Group|Haymarket Publications]]|access-date=18 October 2013|archive-date=16 October 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131016000326/http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/110665|url-status=live}}</ref> He stalled at the start of the main race but went on to finish tenth.

==== 2014: Maiden title in FIA European F3 ====
Ocon continued his collaboration with Prema into the [[2014 FIA Formula 3 European Championship]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.formularapida.net/news/exclusive-esteban-ocon-in-f3-with-prema-powerteam-for-2014/|title=Esteban Ocon in F3 with Prema Powerteam for 2014|last=Vendrell|first=Arnau Viñals|date=19 October 2013|publisher=formularapida.net|access-date=20 October 2013|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131022201528/http://www.formularapida.net/news/exclusive-esteban-ocon-in-f3-with-prema-powerteam-for-2014/|archive-date=22 October 2013}}</ref> He topped the standings at the first round at [[Silverstone Circuit]] and remained in the lead of the championship for the rest of the season.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.paddockscout.com/verstappen-claims-ninth-win-as-ocon-is-crowned-champion/|title=Verstappen claims ninth win as Ocon is crowned champion|last=Khorounzhiy|first=Valentin|date=18 October 2014|publisher=Paddock Scout|access-date=18 October 2014|archive-date=20 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201020051612/https://www.paddockscout.com/verstappen-claims-ninth-win-as-ocon-is-crowned-champion|url-status=live}}</ref> With two rounds to spare, he made a brief appearance in the [[2014 Formula Renault 3.5 Series]] with [[Comtec Racing]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/115774|title=Lotus F1 junior, European F3 leader Esteban Ocon makes FR3.5 debut|last=Simmons|first=Marcus|work=[[Autosport]]|publisher=[[Haymarket Media Group|Haymarket Publications]]|date=8 September 2014|access-date=19 October 2014|archive-date=27 August 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160827091131/http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/115774|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon was crowned FIA Formula 3 European champion with three races remaining, ahead of [[Tom Blomqvist]] and [[Max Verstappen]]. He finished on the podium in twenty-one of the thirty-three races, winning nine, and recorded fifteen pole positions.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/formula-european-masters/news/ocon-claims-title-verstappen-wins-race-at-imola/457500/|date=13 October 2014|title=Ocon claims title, Verstappen wins race at Imola|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100738/https://www.motorsport.com/formula-european-masters/news/ocon-claims-title-verstappen-wins-race-at-imola/457500/|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon made a second appearance at the [[2014 Macau Grand Prix|Macau Grand Prix in 2014]]. He qualified fourth for the main race but was eliminated by a multi-car collision on the first lap.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f3/news/rosenqvist-victorious-at-macau-458828/458828/|date=14 November 2014|title=Rosenqvist victorious at Macau|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100748/https://www.motorsport.com/f3/news/rosenqvist-victorious-at-macau-458828/458828/|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== GP3 Series (2015) ===
Ocon moved to the [[GP3 Series]] for [[2015 GP3 Series|2015]] with [[ART Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Simmons|first=Marcus|url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/esteban-ocon-completes-move-into-gp3-with-art-5009908/5009908/|date=11 March 2015|title=Esteban Ocon completes move into GP3 with ART|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Autosport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100735/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/esteban-ocon-completes-move-into-gp3-with-art-5009908/5009908/|url-status=live}}</ref> Despite only scoring one race victory (two other victories were denied due to penalties),<ref>{{Cite web|last=Bradley|first=Charkes|url=https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/barcelona-gp3-ocon-dominates-season-opener/568105/|date=9 May 2015|title=Barcelona GP3: Ocon dominates season opener|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100748/https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/barcelona-gp3-ocon-dominates-season-opener/568105/|url-status=live}}</ref> he won the championship by eight points ahead of [[Luca Ghiotto]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Khorounzhiy|first=Valentin|url=https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/abu-dhabi-gp3-ocon-crowned-champion-as-palou-takes-maiden-win/660598/|date=29 November 2015|title=Abu Dhabi GP3: Ocon crowned champion as Palou takes maiden win|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100735/https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/abu-dhabi-gp3-ocon-crowned-champion-as-palou-takes-maiden-win/660598/|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon recorded three pole positions and fourteen podium finishes (including nine consecutive second-places) from eighteen races.

=== DTM (2016) ===
Ocon drove for [[Mercedes-Benz in motorsport|Mercedes-Benz]] in the first ten races of the [[2016 Deutsche Tourenwagen Masters|2016 DTM season]], alongside his Formula One reserve driver role at [[Renault in Formula One|Renault]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=on poised for Renault reserve role|date=2 February 2016|url=https://f1i.com/news/40315-ocon-poised-for-renault-reserve-role.html|access-date=29 May 2023|language=en|archive-date=1 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230701110842/https://f1i.com/news/40315-ocon-poised-for-renault-reserve-role.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Elizalde|first=Pablo|url=https://www.motorsport.com/dtm/news/mercedes-confirms-ocon-s-dtm-move-672766/672766/|date=11 February 2016|title=Mercedes confirms Ocon's DTM move|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100735/https://www.motorsport.com/dtm/news/mercedes-confirms-ocon-s-dtm-move-672766/672766/|url-status=live}}</ref> He scored two points finishing ninth in the first race at [[Circuit Zandvoort]], before he was promoted to a Formula 1 race seat. He was replaced by [[Felix Rosenqvist]] following his promotion.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Khorounzhiy|first=Valentin|url=https://www.motorsport.com/dtm/news/rosenqvist-to-replace-ocon-for-dtm-round-in-moscow-806322/806322/|date=10 August 2016|title=Rosenqvist to replace Ocon for DTM round in Moscow|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100740/https://www.motorsport.com/dtm/news/rosenqvist-to-replace-ocon-for-dtm-round-in-moscow-806322/806322/|url-status=live}}</ref>

== Formula One career ==
[[File:Esteban Ocon - Mercedes (32729175350).jpg|thumb|Ocon driving the [[Mercedes F1 W07 Hybrid]]|left]]
Ocon's first experience of a Formula One car was on 22 October 2014, driving the [[Lotus E20]] at [[Circuit Ricardo Tormo]] as part of a two-day test for [[Lotus F1 Team]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/esteban-ocon-completes-lotus-f1-test/457880/|title=Esteban Ocon completes Lotus F1 test|website=motorsport.com|date=23 October 2014|access-date=6 January 2020|archive-date=10 February 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220210030815/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/esteban-ocon-completes-lotus-f1-test/457880/|url-status=live}}</ref> A week later, he completed a test in the [[Ferrari F10]] at [[Fiorano Circuit]] as a prize for his FIA Formula 3 European title.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/headlines/2014/10/Ferrari-impressed-by-Ocon-after-Fiorano-test.html|title=Ferrari impressed by Ocon after Fiorano test|website=formula1.com|date=30 October 2014|accessdate=7 August 2023|archive-date=7 August 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230807074922/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/headlines/2014/10/Ferrari-impressed-by-Ocon-after-Fiorano-test.html|url-status=live}}</ref> In November, Ocon made his Grand Prix weekend debut for Lotus during the first practice session at the [[2014 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|Abu Dhabi Grand Prix]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2014/races/916/abu-dhabi/practice-1.html|title=2014 Formula 1 Etihad Airways Abu Dhabi Grand Prix – Practice 1|website=formula1.com|date=21 November 2014|access-date=6 January 2020|archive-date=22 June 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190622154701/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2014/races/916/abu-dhabi/practice-1.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

In May 2015, Ocon was called up by [[Force India]] to drive at the post-race test in [[Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya|Barcelona]], after [[Pascal Wehrlein]] was forced to withdraw due to illness.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/headlines/2015/5/ocon-to-get-force-india-test-outing-on-wednesday.html|title=Ocon to get Force India test outing on Wednesday|website=formula1.com|date=12 May 2015|access-date=6 January 2020|archive-date=11 August 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200811043906/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/headlines/2015/5/ocon-to-get-force-india-test-outing-on-wednesday.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Prior to him claiming the GP3 title, it was announced that Ocon would enter the [[Mercedes Junior Team]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.racefans.net/2015/05/07/ocon-joins-mercedes-young-driver-roster/|title=Ocon joins Mercedes' young driver roster|website=RaceFans|last=Collantine|first=Keith|date=7 May 2015|access-date=6 September 2024}}</ref> In February 2016, it was announced that Ocon would also act as reserve driver for the [[Renault in Formula One|Renault Sport F1]] team for the {{F1|2016}} season.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/122669|title=Esteban Ocon set to get Renault Formula 1 reserve role for 2016|last=Parkes|first=Ian|work=[[Autosport]]|date=2 February 2016|access-date=2 February 2016|archive-date=18 October 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161018134301/http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/122669|url-status=live}}</ref> He took part in Friday practice sessions at four Grands Prix for the team.

=== Manor (2016) ===
[[File:Esteban Ocon 2016 Malaysia FP3.jpg|thumb|Ocon driving for [[Manor Racing|Manor]] at the [[2016 Malaysian Grand Prix]]]]
On 10 August 2016, [[Rio Haryanto]] was dropped from the [[Glossary of motorsport terms#B|backmarker]] [[Manor Racing]] team after his sponsors had failed to meet their contractual obligations. Ocon was named as his replacement for the second half of the season, driving alongside Pascal Wehrlein.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Barretto|first1=Lawrence|title=Manor F1 team replaces Rio Haryanto with Esteban Ocon|url=http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/125650/manor-replaces-haryanto-with-ocon|website=autosport.com|access-date=10 August 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160810091847/http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/125650/manor-replaces-haryanto-with-ocon|archive-date=10 August 2016|date=10 August 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last1=Morlidge|first1=Matt|title=Esteban Ocon steps up to replace Rio Haryanto at Manor|url=http://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/10530436/esteban-ocon-steps-up-to-replace-rio-haryanto-at-manor|publisher=Sky Sports|access-date=10 August 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160810091556/http://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/10530436/esteban-ocon-steps-up-to-replace-rio-haryanto-at-manor|archive-date=10 August 2016|date=10 August 2016}}</ref> Ocon made his Formula One debut at the {{F1 GP|2016|Belgian}}, finishing sixteenth.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Khorounzhiy|first=Valentin|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/wehrlein-qualifying-gap-to-ocon-shows-haryanto-was-underrated-810816/810816/|date=28 August 2016|title=Wehrlein: Qualifying gap to Ocon shows Haryanto was "underrated"|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529062043/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/wehrlein-qualifying-gap-to-ocon-shows-haryanto-was-underrated-810816/810816/|url-status=live}}</ref> He earned his best result of twelfth in the rain-affected [[2016 Brazilian Grand Prix|Brazilian Grand Prix]], dropping out of the points positions on the final lap.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/felipe-nasrs-brazilian-bonanza-set-to-inject-e35m-to-saubers-f1-bank-balance/3221427/|date=15 November 2016|title=Felipe Nasr's Brazilian bonanza set to inject €35m to Sauber's F1 bank balance|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529062040/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/felipe-nasrs-brazilian-bonanza-set-to-inject-e35m-to-saubers-f1-bank-balance/3221427/|url-status=live}}</ref> This result placed Ocon 23rd in the Drivers' Championship, ahead of Haryanto.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2016 Driver Standings|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2016/drivers.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=1 July 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160701134749/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2016/drivers.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Force India (2017–2018) ===
==== 2017 season ====
[[File:Esteban Ocon Chinese GP 2017.jpg|thumb|Ocon driving for [[Force India]] at the [[2017 Chinese Grand Prix]]]]
[[File:Esteban Ocon 2017 Malaysia 1.jpg|thumb|150px|left|Ocon in 2017]]
On 10 November 2016, [[Force India]] announced that they had signed Ocon for the {{F1|2017}} season as part of his multi-year contract with [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]], with [[Sergio Pérez]] as his new teammate.<ref name="motorsport.com">{{cite news|url=http://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/force-india-signs-ocon-on-multi-year-deal-847808/|title=Force India signs Ocon on multi-year deal|publisher=motorsport.com|access-date=10 November 2016|archive-date=5 July 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180705003712/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/force-india-signs-ocon-on-multi-year-deal-847808/|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon scored his first Formula One point in his first race for Force India at the {{F1 GP|2017|Australian}},<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://autoweek.com/article/formula-one/force-india-scores-top-ten-double-f1-opener-australia|title=Force India scores top-10 double at F1 opener in Australia|work=Autoweek|access-date=26 March 2017|archive-date=26 March 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170326144611/http://autoweek.com/article/formula-one/force-india-scores-top-ten-double-f1-opener-australia|url-status=live}}</ref> and scored points at the next four races including fifth place at the {{F1 GP|2017|Spanish}}.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/spanish-gp-top-10-quotes-after-race-906114/906114/|date=14 May 2017|title=Spanish GP: Top 10 quotes after race|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071847/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/spanish-gp-top-10-quotes-after-race-906114/906114/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Following a twelfth place finish at the {{F1 GP|2017|Monaco}},<ref>{{Cite web|last=Cooper|first=Adam|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/monaco-not-so-bad-for-force-india-despite-non-score-913847/913847/|date=3 June 2017|title=Monaco "not so bad" for Force India despite non-score|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071851/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/monaco-not-so-bad-for-force-india-despite-non-score-913847/913847/|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon recorded twelve consecutive points finishes but was often involved in incidents with teammate Pérez. At the {{F1 GP|2017|Canadian}}, Pérez ignored requests from the team to let Ocon past to challenge [[Daniel Ricciardo]] for third place.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Noble|first=Jonathan|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-force-india-rules-engagement-canada-spat-917698/917698/|date=12 June 2017|title=Force India to review rules of engagement after Canada spat|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071850/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-force-india-rules-engagement-canada-spat-917698/917698/|url-status=live}}</ref> The two drivers collided at the {{F1 GP|2017|Azerbaijan}}, forcing Pérez into retirement and giving Ocon a puncture.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Bradley|first=Charles|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/F1-perez-force-india-ocon-923369/923369/|date=26 June 2017|title=Perez slams Force India teammate Ocon over collision|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071849/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/F1-perez-force-india-ocon-923369/923369/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Noble|first=Jonathan|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/perez-ocon-to-be-told-baku-clash-was-unacceptable-923587/923587/|date=26 June 2017|title=Perez/Ocon to be told Baku clash was "unacceptable"|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071847/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/perez-ocon-to-be-told-baku-clash-was-unacceptable-923587/923587/|url-status=live}}</ref> They made contact again at the {{F1 GP|2017|Belgian}}, where Ocon was squeezed towards a wall leading up to the Eau Rouge complex. Ocon later remarked that he was "furious" with Pérez and that he "risked [their] lives". Force India team owner [[Vijay Mallya]] stated that the repeated incidents were "very concerning" and that he would enforce [[team orders]] thereon.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/41068207|title=Belgian Grand Prix: Esteban Ocon says team-mate 'risked our lives'|website=[[BBC Sport]]|first=Andrew|last=Benson|date=27 August 2017|access-date=14 March 2021|archive-date=31 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201031100457/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/41068207|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Barretto|first=Lawrence|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/force-india-perez-ocon-racing-each-other-belgian-gp-crash-945796/3042834/|date=27 August 2017|title=Perez and Ocon no longer free to race - Force India|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071849/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/force-india-perez-ocon-racing-each-other-belgian-gp-crash-945796/3042834/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Ocon started the {{F1 GP|2017|Italian}} in third place after the [[Red Bull Racing|Red Bull]] drivers faced penalties, the highest grid position of his career.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Bradley|first=Charles|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-italian-monza-third-podium-948416/3044063/|date=3 September 2017|title=Third-placed starter Ocon declares: "I want my podium"|access-date=|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071852/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-italian-monza-third-podium-948416/3044063/|url-status=live}}</ref> He went on to finish the race sixth.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/italian-gp-top-10-quotes-after-race-949069/3044419/|date=3 September 2017|title=Italian GP: Top 10 quotes after race|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071848/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/italian-gp-top-10-quotes-after-race-949069/3044419/|url-status=live}}</ref> He spent much of the {{F1 GP|2017|Mexican}} in third place and eventually finished fifth.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Thukral|first=Rachit|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/force-india-virtual-safety-car-cost-us-mexico-podium-973211/1375108/|date=31 October 2017|title=Force India: Virtual safety car cost us Mexico podium|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071844/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/force-india-virtual-safety-car-cost-us-mexico-podium-973211/1375108/|url-status=live}}</ref> His streak of finishing twenty-seven consecutive races ended at the {{F1 GP|2017|Brazilian}}, where he collided with [[Romain Grosjean]] on the first lap.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Elizalde|first=Pablo|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/grosjean-struggling-to-understand-penalty-ocon-977966/1378161/|date=13 November 2017|title=Grosjean "struggling to understand" Ocon clash penalty|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071845/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/grosjean-struggling-to-understand-penalty-ocon-977966/1378161/|url-status=live}}</ref> He finished his first full season in Formula One eighth in the drivers' championship, scoring 87 points to Pérez's 100.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2017 Driver Standings|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2017/drivers.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=23 October 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171023174116/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2017/drivers.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2018 season ====
[[File:Canadian F1 Grand Prix (42908105521).jpg|thumb|right|Ocon at the [[2018 Canadian Grand Prix]]]]
Ocon continued alongside Pérez at Force India in {{F1|2018}}. Ocon's first points of the season came with a tenth-place finish at the {{F1 GP|2018|Bahrain}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 1 2018 Gulf Air Bahrain Grand Prix - Race Result|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2018/races/980/bahrain/race-result.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=10 April 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180410131417/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2018/races/980/bahrain/race-result.html|url-status=live}}</ref> At the {{F1 GP|2018|Azerbaijan}}, he was involved in a first-lap collision with [[Kimi Räikkönen]] that ended his race, whilst teammate Pérez went on to claim a podium finish.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lewis Hamilton wins chaotic Azerbaijan Grand Prix as Red Bulls collide: F1 – as it happened|date=29 August 2018|url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2018/apr/29/azerbaijan-grand-prix-f1-formula-one-live|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[The Guardian]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071844/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2018/apr/29/azerbaijan-grand-prix-f1-formula-one-live|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon retired with an oil leak at the next race, the {{F1 GP|2018|Spanish}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2018 Spanish Grand Prix report|date=14 May 2018|url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/2018-spanish-grand-prix-report/|access-date=29 May 2023|website=motorsportmagazine.com|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071847/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/2018-spanish-grand-prix-report/|url-status=live}}</ref> He recorded five more points finishes before the summer break, but retired from his home race, the {{F1 GP|2018|French}}, after a first-lap collision with [[Pierre Gasly]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Khorounzhiy|first=Valentin|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-gasly-reprimanded-for-french-gp-crash-1047458/3128816/|date=25 June 2018|title=Ocon, Gasly reprimanded for French GP crash|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071846/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-gasly-reprimanded-for-french-gp-crash-1047458/3128816/|url-status=live}}</ref>

After Force India's financial collapse and the purchasing of its assets by Canadian businessman [[Lawrence Stroll]] – father of [[Williams Grand Prix Engineering|Williams]] driver [[Lance Stroll]] – during the summer break, the new owners confirmed that Ocon and Pérez would remain with the team for the rest of the season. It was later revealed that Ocon had an "informal agreement" to join [[Renault in Formula One|Renault]] for {{F1|2019}} before the team unexpectedly signed Daniel Ricciardo, leaving Ocon's future in doubt.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/45522631|title=Singapore GP: Toto Wolff criticises Renault over Esteban Ocon U-turn|website=bbc.co.uk|date=14 September 2018|access-date=6 January 2020|archive-date=13 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200713094846/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/45522631|url-status=live}}</ref>

At [[Racing Point Force India]]'s first race, the {{F1 GP|2018|Belgian}}, Ocon achieved the joint-highest starting position of his career with third and went on to finish sixth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon hails 'awesome' P3 after 'maximising potential' in qualifying|date=25 August 2018|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-hails-awesome-p3-after-maximising-potential-in-qualifying.4vNVtvtHu0MECMQWSM6qCy.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071847/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-hails-awesome-p3-after-maximising-potential-in-qualifying.4vNVtvtHu0MECMQWSM6qCy.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Beer|first=Matt|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-i-needed-one-more-metre-to-lead-race/3165797/|date=27 August 2018|title=Ocon: I needed one more metre to lead race|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529071854/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-i-needed-one-more-metre-to-lead-race/3165797/|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon and Pérez collided on the first lap of the {{F1 GP|2018|Singapore}}, causing Ocon to crash into a wall and end his race. The team described the collision as "unacceptable" and banned the drivers from racing each other. Pérez later apologised for his role in the accident.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11491892/force-india-slam-unacceptable-sergio-perez-esteban-ocon-crash|title=Force India slam 'unacceptable' Sergio Perez-Esteban Ocon crash|website=skysports.com|date=6 December 2018|access-date=6 January 2020|archive-date=18 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201218151655/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11491892/force-india-slam-unacceptable-sergio-perez-esteban-ocon-crash|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon was disqualified from eighth place at the {{F1 GP|2018|United States}} after his car was found to have exceeded fuel flow limits.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon and Magnussen lose points after US Grand Prix disqualifications|date=21 August 2018|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-and-magnussen-lose-points-after-us-grand-prix-disqualifications.6yGjSpkMqQiis8mWqiIu00.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=9 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201109021506/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-and-magnussen-lose-points-after-us-grand-prix-disqualifications.6yGjSpkMqQiis8mWqiIu00.html|url-status=live}}</ref> At the {{F1 GP|2018|Brazilian}}, he collided with race leader [[Max Verstappen]] whilst attempting to un-lap himself, damaging both cars. Both drivers were able to continue racing and Ocon received a ten-second stop-and-go penalty for the incident.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/brazilian-gp-hamilton-verstappen-ocon/3212168/|title=Brazilian GP: Hamilton wins after Ocon spins Verstappen|last=Mitchell|first=Scott|work=motorsport.com|date=11 November 2018|access-date=11 November 2018|archive-date=27 August 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190827102928/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/brazilian-gp-hamilton-verstappen-ocon/3212168/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.pitpass.com/63499/Ocon-penalised-for-Verstappen-clash|title=Ocon penalised for Verstappen clash|work=pitpass.com|date=11 November 2018|access-date=11 November 2018|archive-date=27 August 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190827102924/https://www.pitpass.com/63499/Ocon-penalised-for-Verstappen-clash|url-status=live}}</ref> They argued just after the race (in which Verstappen finished second) and pushed each other several times.<!-- The cited source states that they "exchanged pushes" - i.e. they pushed each other. --><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.verstappen-and-ocon-in-war-of-words-over-race-defining-interlagos-clash.5wMwoPg2XKysWwEsQiEwsu.html|title=Verstappen and Ocon in war of words over race-defining Interlagos clash|date=11 November 2018|access-date=29 November 2019|website=formula1.com|archive-date=4 May 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190504133429/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.verstappen-and-ocon-in-war-of-words-over-race-defining-interlagos-clash.5wMwoPg2XKysWwEsQiEwsu.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Both drivers were summoned by the [[Federation Internationale de l'Automobile|FIA]] and Verstappen was ordered to undertake two days of public service "at the discretion of the FIA" for making deliberate physical contact with Ocon.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/verstappen-ocon-community-service-brazil/3212401/|title=Verstappen gets "public service" punishment for Ocon shoves|last=Freeman|first=Glenn|work=motorsport.com|date=11 November 2018|access-date=11 November 2018|archive-date=27 August 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190827102924/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/verstappen-ocon-community-service-brazil/3212401/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Ocon finished the season twelfth in the drivers' championship, scoring 49 points to Pérez's 62.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2018 Driver Standings|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2018/drivers.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=19 December 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181219025934/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2018/drivers.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Mercedes reserve driver (2019) ===
For the 2019 season, Ocon was replaced at Racing Point by [[Lance Stroll]]. There was an agreement in principle for Ocon to move to [[Renault in Formula One|Renault]], this subsequently fell through.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Why Mercedes could lose out f1 silly season |date=20 August 2018 |url=https://www.crash.net/f1/feature/903525/1/why-mercedes-could-lose-out-f1-s-silly-season }}</ref> Ocon joined Mercedes as their reserve driver for {{F1|2019}} to drive their [[Mercedes AMG F1 W10 EQ Power+]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Noble |first1=Jonathan |last2=Beer |first2=Matt |title=Esteban Ocon gets 2019 Mercedes F1 reserve driver role |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/140281/ocon-gets-mercedes-reserve-role-for-2019 |website=autosport.com |access-date=30 November 2018 |date=23 November 2018 |archive-date=30 November 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181130202005/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/140281/ocon-gets-mercedes-reserve-role-for-2019 |url-status=live }}</ref> Ocon did not take part in a Grand Prix weekend during the year. He claimed to have been in discussions with Mercedes for the {{F1|2020}} season, remarking that he was "very close" to replacing [[Valtteri Bottas]] at the team. Mercedes ultimately decided to continue with Bottas.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.planetf1.com/news/ocon-was-close-to-mercedes/|title=Ocon was 'very close' to 2020 Mercedes seat|website=planetf1.com|date=21 January 2020|access-date=14 March 2021|archive-date=17 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210617232947/https://www.planetf1.com/news/ocon-was-close-to-mercedes/|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Renault / Alpine (2020–2024) ===
==== 2020: Maiden podium ====
[[File:Esteban Ocon, 2020 pre-season testing.jpg|thumb|left|Ocon during [[2020 Formula One pre-season testing|pre-season testing in 2020]]]]
Ocon joined [[Renault in F1|Renault]] for 2020, signing a two-year contract and marking his return to Formula One as a full-time driver. He replaced [[Nico Hülkenberg]] and partnered with [[Daniel Ricciardo]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-to-replace-hulkenberg-at-renault/4523388/|title=Ocon to replace Hulkenberg at Renault|website=www.motorsport.com|date=29 August 2019 |language=en|access-date=29 August 2019|archive-date=29 August 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190829121235/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-to-replace-hulkenberg-at-renault/4523388/|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon qualified fourteenth on his Renault debut at the [[2020 Austrian Grand Prix|Austrian Grand Prix]] and finished eighth.<ref>{{Cite web|title='We need to make our life easier on Saturdays' says Ocon after top 10 finish on F1 return|date=5 July 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.we-need-to-make-our-life-easier-on-saturdays-says-ocon-after-top-10-finish.2LtpDoWQqSoT3IixPJegP5.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529090135/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.we-need-to-make-our-life-easier-on-saturdays-says-ocon-after-top-10-finish.2LtpDoWQqSoT3IixPJegP5.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He was running in seventh place at the {{F1 GP|2020|Styrian}} when he retired with a cooling issue.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Cooper|first=Adam|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/renault-radiator-failure-ocon-styria/4833270/|date=13 July 2020|title=Renault seeks urgent solution after second radiator failure|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529084633/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/renault-radiator-failure-ocon-styria/4833270/|url-status=live}}</ref> At the [[70th Anniversary Grand Prix]], he was issued a grid penalty after impeding [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]] in qualifying and started fourteenth,<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon handed three-place penalty for impeding Russell in Q1 at Silverstone|date=8 August 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-handed-three-place-penalty-for-impeding-russell-in-q1-at-silverstone.HbFSRVUKK0xEc8zuMKxGS.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529101651/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-handed-three-place-penalty-for-impeding-russell-in-q1-at-silverstone.HbFSRVUKK0xEc8zuMKxGS.html|url-status=live}}</ref> but improved to finish eighth in the race.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon keen to 'fight with the bigger boys' after 'fun' drive to P8|date=10 August 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-keen-to-fight-with-the-bigger-boys-after-fun-drive-to-p8.5FKyFyJAkLTDxKiKsUv7uj.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529101653/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-keen-to-fight-with-the-bigger-boys-after-fun-drive-to-p8.5FKyFyJAkLTDxKiKsUv7uj.html|url-status=live}}</ref> His best race finish since 2017 came at the {{F1 GP|2020|Belgian}}, where he qualified sixth and finished fifth behind teammate Ricciardo.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ricciardo 'stoked' with P4 as he leads Renault's best qualifying of 2020|date=29 August 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ricciardo-stoked-with-p4-as-he-leads-renaults-best-qualifying-of-2020.5dbbfeo74Ku8QpUjLiS2MH.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529094647/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ricciardo-stoked-with-p4-as-he-leads-renaults-best-qualifying-of-2020.5dbbfeo74Ku8QpUjLiS2MH.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon hails 'fantastic race' after last-lap pass on Red Bull's Albon to secure P5|date=30 August 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-hails-fantastic-race-after-last-lap-pass-on-red-bulls-albon-to-secure.1xhLaVyIA8D84nfynw5sEc.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529104701/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-hails-fantastic-race-after-last-lap-pass-on-red-bulls-albon-to-secure.1xhLaVyIA8D84nfynw5sEc.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

Ocon's brakes caught fire during a [[safety car]] period at the {{F1 GP|2020|Tuscan}}. The team was unable to repair the damage during the [[Racing flags#Red flag|red flag]] period which occurred soon after, and Ocon failed to make the restart.<ref>{{Cite web|title='There will be more opportunities for us' says Ocon after brake fire rules him out of Mugello race|date=14 September 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.there-will-be-more-opportunities-for-us-says-ocon-after-brake-fire-rules-him.7JQ4v0Cn5LIbEu3t1yPOn3.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529094647/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.there-will-be-more-opportunities-for-us-says-ocon-after-brake-fire-rules-him.7JQ4v0Cn5LIbEu3t1yPOn3.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He experienced further mechanical retirements at the [[2020 Eifel Grand Prix|Eifel Grand Prix]] and the [[2020 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix|Emilia Romagna Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Renault 'definitely in hunt for P3', says Ricciardo as drivers hope for more podiums in 2020|date=22 October 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.renault-definitely-in-hunt-for-p3-says-ricciardo-as-drivers-hope-for-more.3pdHEswiTgbH98fXDI75mT.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529103157/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.renault-definitely-in-hunt-for-p3-says-ricciardo-as-drivers-hope-for-more.3pdHEswiTgbH98fXDI75mT.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Renault apologise to Ocon after third retirement in five races at Imola|date=4 November 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.renault-apologise-to-ocon-after-third-retirement-in-five-races-at-imola.6Y3Ffb1xFYhcI3GtzmXSyX.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529051207/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.renault-apologise-to-ocon-after-third-retirement-in-five-races-at-imola.6Y3Ffb1xFYhcI3GtzmXSyX.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified seventh for the {{F1 GP|2020|Turkish}} and made his way into third place by the first corner, but separate collisions with Ricciardo and Valtteri Bottas resulted in him finishing outside the points in eleventh place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Seventh-place Ocon hoped for thunderstorms after briefly topping Q1 with 'lap of the season'|date=14 November 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.seventh-place-ocon-hoped-for-thunderstorms-after-briefly-topping-q1-with-lap.5hs2O3EdeqOVJjhgW082PQ.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529101654/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.seventh-place-ocon-hoped-for-thunderstorms-after-briefly-topping-q1-with-lap.5hs2O3EdeqOVJjhgW082PQ.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title='Gutted' Ocon says he had pace for top-five finish in Turkish GP without pair of Lap 1 spins|date=17 November 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.gutted-ocon-says-he-had-pace-for-top-five-finish-in-turkish-gp-without-pair.1yvrQiekSo1N9zW6mGm3t4.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529094645/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.gutted-ocon-says-he-had-pace-for-top-five-finish-in-turkish-gp-without-pair.1yvrQiekSo1N9zW6mGm3t4.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

Ocon started eleventh at the {{F1 GP|2020|Sakhir}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title='We had top-five in us' says Ricciardo as he prepares to go on the offensive in Sakhir GP|date=5 December 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.we-had-top-five-in-us-says-ricciardo-as-he-prepares-to-go-on-the-offensive.OiNJXoNx0EbC9blXAEGfq.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529094646/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.we-had-top-five-in-us-says-ricciardo-as-he-prepares-to-go-on-the-offensive.OiNJXoNx0EbC9blXAEGfq.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He had improved to fifth place by lap 54 of 87, assisted by collisions on the opening lap and drivers making second pit stops. A [[virtual safety car]] (VSC) period followed, which third-placed [[Carlos Sainz Jr.]] and fourth-placed Ricciardo attempted to take advantage of by entering the pits. However, the VSC period ended whilst they were in the pit lane, nullifying their advantage and promoting Ocon to third place. He was soon overtaken by Sergio Pérez, however pit stop issues for the leading Mercedes cars allowed Ocon to claim his first Formula One podium by finishing second, Renault's best race result since {{F1|2010}}.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/10-things-we-learned-from-the-2020-sakhir-grand-prix-4976520/4976520/|work=Autosport|title=10 things we learned from the 2020 Sakhir Grand Prix|date=7 December 2020|access-date=11 May 2023|last=Smith|first=Luke|archive-date=11 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230511075206/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/10-things-we-learned-from-the-2020-sakhir-grand-prix-4976520/4976520/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Delighted Ocon reflects on 'difficult journey' to maiden podium after P2 finish in Sakhir|date=6 December 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.delighted-ocon-reflects-on-difficult-journey-to-maiden-podium-after-p2.TUcr53hXL3552oM7XrDte.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529093142/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.delighted-ocon-reflects-on-difficult-journey-to-maiden-podium-after-p2.TUcr53hXL3552oM7XrDte.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He ended the season twelfth in the drivers' championship, scoring 62 points to Ricciardo's 119.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2020 Driver Standings|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2020/drivers.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|archive-date=28 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210128035850/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2020/drivers.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2021: Maiden victory ====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2021 Nr. 31 Ocon.jpg|thumb|Ocon at the [[2021 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
Renault rebranded as [[Alpine F1 Team]] for the {{F1|2021}} season. The team signed two-time world champion [[Fernando Alonso]] to partner Ocon after Daniel Ricciardo left for [[McLaren]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Fernando Alonso to make sensational return to F1 with Renault in 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.fernando-alonso-to-make-sensational-return-to-f1-with-renault-in-2021.70HoQCymKIElIDzHFXkaBB.html|access-date=20 September 2020|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=2 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201002160207/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.fernando-alonso-to-make-sensational-return-to-f1-with-renault-in-2021.70HoQCymKIElIDzHFXkaBB.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=McLaren Racing - Daniel Ricciardo to drive for McLaren from 2021|url=https://www.mclaren.com/racing/team/daniel-ricciardo-drive-mclaren-2021/|access-date=20 September 2020|website=www.mclaren.com|language=en|archive-date=25 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200925100451/https://www.mclaren.com/racing/team/daniel-ricciardo-drive-mclaren-2021/|url-status=live}}</ref> In the team's first race as Alpine, the {{F1 GP|2021|Bahrain}}, Ocon was [[Rear-end collision|rear-ended]] by [[Sebastian Vettel]] in the [[Aston Martin Cognizant Formula One Team|Aston Martin]]. Ocon finished the race thirteenth and Vettel later apologised for the incident.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon confirms Vettel apologised for collision|url=https://www.msn.com/en-gb/sport/formula1/ocon-confirms-vettel-apologised-for-collision/ar-BB1f5ZEt|access-date=29 April 2021|website=www.msn.com|language=en|archive-date=29 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210429082942/https://www.msn.com/en-gb/sport/formula1/ocon-confirms-vettel-apologised-for-collision/ar-BB1f5ZEt|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon was classified ninth at the {{F1 GP|2021|Emilia Romagna}} ahead of Alonso in tenth,<ref>{{Cite web|title=Esteban Ocon 'maximised' Alpine's potential in Imola qualifying|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/video/2021/4/Esteban_Ocon_%27maximised%27_Alpine%27s_potential_in_Imola_qualifying.html|access-date=29 April 2021|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210429082942/https://www.formula1.com/en/video/2021/4/Esteban_Ocon_%27maximised%27_Alpine%27s_potential_in_Imola_qualifying.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Raikkonen loses points after post-race penalty at Imola|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/raikkonen-loses-points-after-post-race-imola-penalty/6334393/|access-date=29 April 2021|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|date=18 April 2021 |language=en|archive-date=25 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210525021858/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/raikkonen-loses-points-after-post-race-imola-penalty/6334393/|url-status=live}}</ref> earning the team their first points under the Alpine name.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon relishes 'fights with Fernando' as Alpine score maiden points of campaign at Imola|date=21 April 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-relishes-fights-with-fernando-as-alpine-score-maiden-points-of-campaign.22mbXbRH0Keb5f0GyjzUsp.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529110207/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-relishes-fights-with-fernando-as-alpine-score-maiden-points-of-campaign.22mbXbRH0Keb5f0GyjzUsp.html|url-status=live}}</ref> His first retirement of the season came at the {{F1 GP|2021|Azerbaijan}} with a turbocharger failure.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Collantine|first=Keith|date=8 June 2021|title=2021 Azerbaijan Grand Prix F1 Star Performers|url=https://www.racefans.net/2021/06/08/2021-azerbaijan-grand-prix-star-performers/|access-date=21 February 2022|website=RaceFans|language=en-GB|archive-date=21 February 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220221102830/https://www.racefans.net/2021/06/08/2021-azerbaijan-grand-prix-star-performers/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 1 Azerbaijan Grand Prix 2021 - Race Result|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2021/races/1068/azerbaijan/race-result.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210329084450/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2021/races/1068/azerbaijan/race-result.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He struggled with tyre wear and finished fourteenth at the [[2021 French Grand Prix|French Grand Prix]],<ref>{{Cite news |url= https://www.reuters.com/article/uk-motor-f1-france-analysis-idINKCN2DW0MC |title= Motor racing-Team by team analysis of the French Grand Prix |date= 20 June 2021 |access-date= 29 June 2021 |work= [[Reuters]] |last1= Baldwin |first1= Alan |last2= Osmond |first2= Ed |archive-date= 29 July 2021 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20210729150318/https://www.reuters.com/article/uk-motor-f1-france-analysis-idINKCN2DW0MC |url-status= live }}</ref> qualified seventeenth for both the [[2021 Styrian Grand Prix|Styrian]] and [[2021 Austrian Grand Prix|Austrian]] Grands Prix and retired from the latter after a first-lap collision with [[Antonio Giovinazzi]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon relieved 'painful' Red Bull Ring double is over after Austrian GP Lap 1 exit extends point-less streak|date=5 July 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-relieved-painful-red-bull-ring-double-is-over-after-austrian-gp-lap-1.2IOBOamvi1uKuKSr28VWI8.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=28 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528193034/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-relieved-painful-red-bull-ring-double-is-over-after-austrian-gp-lap-1.2IOBOamvi1uKuKSr28VWI8.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Prior to the French Grand Prix, it was announced that Ocon had signed a contract extension with Alpine running to the end of 2024.<ref>{{Cite web|date=16 June 2021|title=Esteban Ocon signs bumper three-year contract extension with Alpine|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-esteban-ocon-signs-bumper-three-year-contract-extension-with-alpine.5nWR2pWD1COJzdyB73g8NM.html|url-status=live|access-date=18 June 2021|website=Formula1|language=en|archive-date=16 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210616145008/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-esteban-ocon-signs-bumper-three-year-contract-extension-with-alpine.5nWR2pWD1COJzdyB73g8NM.html}}</ref>

Ocon started eighth at the {{F1 GP|2021|Hungarian}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=QUALIFYING: Hamilton roars to Hungary pole, as Bottas denies Verstappen front-row start|date=31 July 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.qualifying-hamilton-roars-to-hungary-pole-as-bottas-denies-verstappen-front.6UjZ9TXDnFxGSnHd630Lwh.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=4 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204013737/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.qualifying-hamilton-roars-to-hungary-pole-as-bottas-denies-verstappen-front.6UjZ9TXDnFxGSnHd630Lwh.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Multiple collisions ahead saw him promoted to second place at the first corner, which became first place when race leader [[Lewis Hamilton]] pitted for dry-weather tyres one lap later than the rest of the field. Ocon held on to the lead for the remainder of the race, fending off Sebastian Vettel to take his and Alpine's maiden Formula One victory.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Richards|first=Giles|date=1 August 2021|title=Ocon claims Hungarian Grand Prix as Hamilton gets promoted to second|url=http://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/aug/01/esteban-ocon-claims-maiden-f1-win-in-chaotic-hungarian-grand-prix|access-date=21 February 2022|website=the Guardian|language=en|archive-date=24 March 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220324095805/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/aug/01/esteban-ocon-claims-maiden-f1-win-in-chaotic-hungarian-grand-prix|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon thanks Alpine team mate Alonso for 'fighting like a lion' to help him to maiden win in Hungary|date=1 August 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-thanks-alpine-team-mate-alonso-for-fighting-like-a-lion-to-help-him-to.7jzK2CudYsitlEaiveAwXk.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529103158/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-thanks-alpine-team-mate-alonso-for-fighting-like-a-lion-to-help-him-to.7jzK2CudYsitlEaiveAwXk.html|url-status=live}}</ref> This win was followed by points finishes at the next three races. The {{F1 GP|2021|Turkish}} took place in damp conditions and Ocon finished tenth having run the entire race distance on one set of intermediate-weather tyres.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon admits it was a 'risky bet' not to pit in Turkey as Alpine boss says 'we didn't know if he'd make it'|date=13 October 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-admits-it-was-a-risky-bet-not-to-pit-in-turkey-as-alpine-boss-says-we.2R2jvJpVWn4vgHHNi3XzCP.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529113217/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-admits-it-was-a-risky-bet-not-to-pit-in-turkey-as-alpine-boss-says-we.2R2jvJpVWn4vgHHNi3XzCP.html|url-status=live}}</ref> This was the first time a driver had completed a full race distance without making a pit stop since {{F1|1997}}.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-ocons-dangerous-non-stop-strategy-paid-off/6686000/ |title= How Ocon's 'dangerous' non-stop Turkey F1 strategy paid off |last= Cooper |first= Adam |work= [[Autosport]] |date= 13 October 2021 |access-date= 13 October 2021 |archive-date= 13 October 2021 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20211013101518/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-ocons-dangerous-non-stop-strategy-paid-off/6686000/ |url-status= live }}</ref>

A collision with Antonio Giovinazzi at the {{F1 GP|2021|United States}} broke Ocon's front wing and ultimately led to retirement.<ref>{{Cite web|title='Everything that could go wrong did go wrong' says Alpine boss after double DNF in Austin|date=27 October 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.everything-that-could-go-wrong-did-go-wrong-says-alpine-boss-after-double.6zp0a3X9zND99LzQ3VEmIw.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529110205/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.everything-that-could-go-wrong-did-go-wrong-says-alpine-boss-after-double.6zp0a3X9zND99LzQ3VEmIw.html|url-status=live}}</ref> A fifth-place finish at the {{F1 GP|2021|Qatar}} was followed by a near-podium at the {{F1 GP|2021|Saudi Arabian}}; Ocon briefly led the race at its first restart and ran in third place for most of the race, but was passed by [[Valtteri Bottas]] shortly before the chequered flag, finishing just 0.102 seconds behind.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Alonso says first podium since 2014 shows he's moved to 'another level' compared to start of his F1 comeback|date=21 November 2021|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.alonso-says-first-podium-since-2014-shows-hes-moved-to-another-level.27LgwBvkBhzFf80lHZFQJb.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529111712/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.alonso-says-first-podium-since-2014-shows-hes-moved-to-another-level.27LgwBvkBhzFf80lHZFQJb.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon distraught after Bottas denies him Saudi podium – but warns that Alpine becoming 'dangerous' for rivals|date=5 December 2020|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-distraught-after-bottas-denies-him-saudi-podium-but-warns-that-alpine.7yQNP0DVtyYH9hs9HfyxRO.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=30 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230330210005/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-distraught-after-bottas-denies-him-saudi-podium-but-warns-that-alpine.7yQNP0DVtyYH9hs9HfyxRO.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon ended the season eleventh in the drivers' championship, scoring 74 points to Alonso's 81.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2021 Driver Standings|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2021/drivers.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=28 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210328180631/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2021/drivers.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2022 season ====
[[File:Esteban Ocon 2022 Emilia Romagna GP.jpg|thumb|left|Ocon at the [[2022 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix]]]]
Alpine retained Ocon and Alonso for the {{F1|2022}} season.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 F1 GRID: All the drivers and teams racing this season|date=5 January 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.2022-f1-grid-all-the-drivers-and-teams-racing-this-season.3L1E0DrPLfzmN9GNMZcE5m.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=23 February 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220223053853/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.2022-f1-grid-all-the-drivers-and-teams-racing-this-season.3L1E0DrPLfzmN9GNMZcE5m.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon finished seventh at the season-opening {{F1 GP|2022|Bahrain}} despite receiving a penalty for colliding with [[Mick Schumacher]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon pleased to shrug off penalty and lead double-points finish for Alpine|date=22 March 2023|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-pleased-to-shrug-off-penalty-and-lead-double-points-finish-for-alpine.6QmhVNKAS77voVmvhDIT95.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=20 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230320101029/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-pleased-to-shrug-off-penalty-and-lead-double-points-finish-for-alpine.6QmhVNKAS77voVmvhDIT95.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified fifth and finished sixth at the {{F1 GP|2022|Saudi Arabian}} where a close battle with Alonso ended with Ocon being ordered by the team to hold his position.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon eyeing podium after qualifying P5 with 'extremely strong' pace at Jeddah|date=26 March 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-eyeing-podium-after-qualifying-p5-with-extremely-strong-pace-at-jeddah.3rg8RP2aCsAL0YgVQtiH69.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=22 June 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220622174649/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-eyeing-podium-after-qualifying-p5-with-extremely-strong-pace-at-jeddah.3rg8RP2aCsAL0YgVQtiH69.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Mitchell|first=Scott|date=28 March 2022|url=https://the-race.com/formula-1/alpine-only-has-one-regret-about-ferocious-ocon-alonso-fight/|title=Alpine only has one regret about ferocious Ocon/Alonso fight|website=The Race|access-date=28 March 2022|archive-date=28 March 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220328144957/https://the-race.com/formula-1/alpine-only-has-one-regret-about-ferocious-ocon-alonso-fight/|url-status=live}}</ref> A crash in practice for the {{F1 GP|2022|Miami}} forced him to miss qualifying and start last on the grid.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Smith|first=Luke|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-to-miss-miami-f1-qualifying-due-to-cracked-chassis/10300902/|date=8 May 2022|title=Ocon to miss Miami F1 qualifying due to cracked chassis|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529092443/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-to-miss-miami-f1-qualifying-due-to-cracked-chassis/10300902/|url-status=live}}</ref> He recovered in the race to finish ninth and was promoted to eighth when Alonso received a penalty.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Cooper|first=Adam|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/esteban-ocon-miami-gp-f1/10302180/|date=11 May 2022|title=Ocon: Miami F1 eighth place "like a victory" from back of grid|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529092440/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/esteban-ocon-miami-gp-f1/10302180/|url-status=live}}</ref> At the [[2022 Spanish Grand Prix|Spanish Grand Prix]], Ocon qualified twelfth and finished seventh, ahead of Alonso, after holding off the fast-charging [[Lando Norris]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.motorlat.com/notas/id/25429 | title=F1 &#124; Spanish GP &#124; Ocon: P7 "feels like a victory" | date=23 May 2022 | access-date=24 May 2022 | archive-date=1 July 2023 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230701110848/https://www.motorlat.com/notas/f1/25429/f1-spanish-gp-ocon-p7-feels-like-a-victory | url-status=live }}</ref> Ocon finished ninth at the {{F1 GP|2022|Monaco}} but was demoted to twelfth by a penalty for colliding with Lewis Hamilton.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Alonso happy with P7 finish in Monaco after 'tricky race' but Ocon left frustrated by 5s penalty|date=30 May 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.alonso-happy-with-p7-finish-in-monaco-after-tricky-race-but-ocon-left.6NQR7JWq4xonP7gOOtlkbM.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529124727/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.alonso-happy-with-p7-finish-in-monaco-after-tricky-race-but-ocon-left.6NQR7JWq4xonP7gOOtlkbM.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

At the [[2022 British Grand Prix|British Grand Prix]], Ocon qualified fifteenth due to battery issues and retired from the race with a fuel pump problem, despite the significant upgrade packages brought to the [[Alpine A522]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.givemesport.com/88029308-british-gp-esteban-ocon-reveals-battery-issue-behind-p15-in-qualifying|title=British GP: Esteban Ocon reveals battery issue behind P15 in qualifying|date=3 July 2022|access-date=5 July 2022|archive-date=5 July 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220705191219/https://www.givemesport.com/88029308-british-gp-esteban-ocon-reveals-battery-issue-behind-p15-in-qualifying|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Alonso admits he was eyeing podium finish as leaders battled in front of him around Silverstone|date=4 July 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.alonso-admits-he-was-eyeing-podium-finish-as-leaders-battled-around.43ih8MxLSHuNGr9DRfvjr9.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529123223/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.alonso-admits-he-was-eyeing-podium-finish-as-leaders-battled-around.43ih8MxLSHuNGr9DRfvjr9.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Five points finishes followed, including fifth at the {{F1 GP|2022|Austrian}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon hails 'perfect weekend' for Alpine after fifth place finish at Austrian GP|date=10 July 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-hails-perfect-weekend-for-alpine-after-fifth-place-finish-at-austrian.7v1UUOnKNJDPM9UMVI1dDp.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529120228/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-hails-perfect-weekend-for-alpine-after-fifth-place-finish-at-austrian.7v1UUOnKNJDPM9UMVI1dDp.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon qualified fifth at the {{F1 GP|2022|Belgian}} but was demoted to sixteenth by an engine component penalty.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Verstappen, Leclerc and more set for Belgian Grand Prix grid penalties after power unit changes|date=26 August 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.verstappen-leclerc-and-more-set-for-belgian-grand-prix-grid-penalties-after.2XnehWp6I29AdvqnTeyF8P.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=28 August 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220828040116/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.verstappen-leclerc-and-more-set-for-belgian-grand-prix-grid-penalties-after.2XnehWp6I29AdvqnTeyF8P.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He recovered in the race to score points in seventh place.<ref>{{Cite web|title='Frustrated' Alonso relieved to finish Belgian GP strongly, as Ocon praises 'flying' car for recovery from P16|date=29 August 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.frustrated-alonso-relieved-to-finish-belgian-gp-strongly-as-ocon-praises.7xvddpFAiQDHJyJxV4uggC.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529101700/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.frustrated-alonso-relieved-to-finish-belgian-gp-strongly-as-ocon-praises.7xvddpFAiQDHJyJxV4uggC.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He started seventeenth at the {{F1 GP|2022|Singapore}} having experienced brake problems in qualifying and then retired from the race with an engine failure.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.planetf1.com/news/esteban-ocon-brake-problem-singapore/|title=Esteban Ocon confirms 'very big brake problem' behind Q1 exit in Singapore|website=planetf1|first=Jamie|last=Woodhouse|date=1 October 2022|accessdate=8 October 2022|archive-date=8 October 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221008081643/https://www.planetf1.com/news/esteban-ocon-brake-problem-singapore/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Esteban Denied Singapore Score Following Power Unit Failure|date=2 October 2022|url=https://www.esteban-ocon.com/news/esteban-denied-singapore-score-following-power-unit-failure|access-date=29 May 2023|website=esteban-ocon.com|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529092440/https://www.esteban-ocon.com/news/esteban-denied-singapore-score-following-power-unit-failure|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon's best result of the season thus far came at the {{F1 GP|2022|Japanese}}, where he held off Lewis Hamilton to finish fourth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon enjoys 'karting battle' with Hamilton as Alpine reclaim P4 from McLaren with Suzuka points haul|date=10 October 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-enjoys-karting-battle-with-hamilton-as-alpine-reclaim-p4-from-mclaren.6ftaYNRPZ30EQCSqIjGax4.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529100154/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-enjoys-karting-battle-with-hamilton-as-alpine-reclaim-p4-from-mclaren.6ftaYNRPZ30EQCSqIjGax4.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon was eliminated in the first qualifying session and started eighteenth at the [[2022 United States Grand Prix|United States Grand Prix]]; he finished eleventh after taking new [[Formula One engines|power unit]] elements and starting from the pit lane.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Esteban Just Misses Out On Points at COTA Despite Pitlane Start|date=23 October 2022|url=https://www.esteban-ocon.com/news/esteban-just-misses-out-on-points-at-cota-despite-pitlane-start|access-date=29 May 2023|website=esteban-ocon.com|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529092442/https://www.esteban-ocon.com/news/esteban-just-misses-out-on-points-at-cota-despite-pitlane-start|url-status=live}}</ref> He was involved in separate collisions with teammate Alonso in the {{F1 GP|2022|São Paulo}} sprint, with the damage to his car dropping him to seventeenth place.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Noble|first=Jonathan|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-ocon-alonso-unaware-clash-teammate-brazil-sprint/10398978/|date=13 November 2022|title=Ocon unaware of second clash with F1 teammate Alonso in Brazil sprint|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529092440/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-ocon-alonso-unaware-clash-teammate-brazil-sprint/10398978/|url-status=live}}</ref> He recovered to score points in the race.<ref>{{Cite web|title='I think we did everything perfect' – Ocon thrilled after comeback drive helps Alpine extend lead over McLaren|date=15 November 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.i-think-we-did-everything-perfect-ocon-thrilled-after-comeback-drive-helps.3uazlqucgDszzYKgx7C2CE.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529111709/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.i-think-we-did-everything-perfect-ocon-thrilled-after-comeback-drive-helps.3uazlqucgDszzYKgx7C2CE.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

Ocon ended the season eighth in the drivers' championship, equalling his best result previously achieved in 2017. He scored 92 points to Alonso's 81.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Driver Standings|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2022/drivers.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=12 April 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220412090734/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2022/drivers.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2023 season ====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2023 Nr. 31 (1).jpg|thumb|Ocon at the [[2023 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
For {{F1|2023}}, Ocon gained a new teammate in former karting rival Pierre Gasly as Alonso departed to [[Aston Martin in F1|Aston Martin]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Smith|first=Luke|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/fernando-alonso-switches-to-aston-martin-f1-team-from-2023/10347079/|date=1 August 2022|title=Fernando Alonso switches to Aston Martin F1 team from 2023|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=24 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221224065745/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/fernando-alonso-switches-to-aston-martin-f1-team-from-2023/10347079/|url-status=live}}</ref> His training was impacted prior to the start of the season when he got "very sick" with a lung virus.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Smith|first=Luke|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-got-very-sick-in-f1-off-season-due-to-bad-lung-virus/10433258/|date=17 February 2023|title=Ocon got "very sick" in F1 off-season due to bad lung virus|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Motorsport.com]]|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529094200/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ocon-got-very-sick-in-f1-off-season-due-to-bad-lung-virus/10433258/|url-status=live}}</ref>

At the season-opening {{F1 GP|2023|Bahrain}}, Ocon received penalties for being out of position on the grid, failing to serve the penalty correctly and for speeding in the pit lane. He eventually retired from the race with mechanical issues.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.everything-went-wrong-today-says-ocon-after-being-penalised-three-times-and.1Obkye7mOTceYVpzCX9Bp6.html|title='Everything went wrong today' says frustrated Ocon after being penalised three times and retiring early in Bahrain|work=[[Formula 1]]|date=6 March 2023|access-date=6 March 2023|archive-date=6 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230306022140/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.everything-went-wrong-today-says-ocon-after-being-penalised-three-times-and.1Obkye7mOTceYVpzCX9Bp6.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12473/12826969/bahrain-grand-prix-esteban-ocon-equals-unwanted-record-with-three-driving-penalties-before-retiring|title=Bahrain Grand Prix: Esteban Ocon equals unwanted record with three driving penalties before retiring|work=Sky Sports|date=5 March 2023|access-date=6 March 2023|archive-date=6 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230306010744/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12473/12826969/bahrain-grand-prix-esteban-ocon-equals-unwanted-record-with-three-driving-penalties-before-retiring|url-status=live}}</ref> He started sixth and scored his first points of the season at the {{F1 GP|2023|Saudi Arabian}}, finishing eighth. Running in tenth place at the final restart of the {{F1 GP|2023|Australian}}, Ocon was involved in a heavy collision with teammate Gasly, who apologised for his role in the incident. Ocon crashed in qualifying at the {{F1 GP|2023|Azerbaijan}}. Alpine then made changes to his car under [[parc fermé]] conditions, forcing him to start the sprint race and the main race from the pit lane.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ocon to start Azerbaijan Sprint and Grand Prix from pit lane after Alpine make parc ferme changes|date=29 April 2023|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-to-start-azerbaijan-sprint-and-grand-prix-from-pit-lane-after-alpine.5SEXnfuFG1TAbaCEqJOssg.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=5 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230505113954/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.ocon-to-start-azerbaijan-sprint-and-grand-prix-from-pit-lane-after-alpine.5SEXnfuFG1TAbaCEqJOssg.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Learning the key as BWT Alpine F1 Team look to finish Baku weekend with points|date=29 April 2023|url=https://www.alpine-cars.co.uk/formula-1/f1-news/sprint-azerbaijan-baku-2023.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=alpinecars.co.uk|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529094157/https://www.alpine-cars.co.uk/formula-1/f1-news/sprint-azerbaijan-baku-2023.html|url-status=live}}</ref> During the race, Ocon ran on the hard tyres until the last lap. Photographers began to enter the pit lane, not realising Ocon was yet to pit, and narrowly avoided being hit by his car.<ref>{{Cite web|title='Absolute shambles': Esteban Ocon almost drives into F1 photographers in near-disaster|date=30 April 2023|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-esteban-ocon-photographers-azerbaijan-baku-b2329771.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[The Independent]]|language=en|archive-date=25 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230525085237/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-esteban-ocon-photographers-azerbaijan-baku-b2329771.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Gasly keen to move on from 'very bad' weekend as Alpine fail to score in Baku|date=2 May 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.gasly-keen-to-move-on-from-very-bad-weekend-as-alpine-fail-to-score-in-baku.7i0fL4Ha0yNXRoj0Pr3Fn2.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=29 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230529123237/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.gasly-keen-to-move-on-from-very-bad-weekend-as-alpine-fail-to-score-in-baku.7i0fL4Ha0yNXRoj0Pr3Fn2.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

Ocon started third at the {{F1 GP|2023|Monaco}} after [[Charles Leclerc]] ahead received a penalty.<ref>{{Cite web|title='It's a hell of a moment for everyone' says 'very pleased' Ocon after qualifying in P4 for Monaco GP|date=27 May 2023|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.its-a-hell-of-a-moment-for-everyone-says-very-pleased-ocon-after-qualifying.7MnG76wkVKXdS17PmEib4W.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=28 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528121343/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.its-a-hell-of-a-moment-for-everyone-says-very-pleased-ocon-after-qualifying.7MnG76wkVKXdS17PmEib4W.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Ocon held off Carlos Sainz Jr. in the first half of the race but lost a place to George Russell during the pit stops. A mistake and a penalty for Russell allowed Ocon back into third place, earning him his third career podium and the ''Driver Of The Day'' award.<ref>{{Cite web|title=DRIVER OF THE DAY: Ocon gets your vote for mighty drive to P3 in Monaco|date=28 May 2023|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.driver-of-the-day-ocon-gets-your-vote-for-mighty-drive-to-p3-in-monaco.4OALiqRbQW3MCAP22BCw7Q.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=28 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528165142/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.driver-of-the-day-ocon-gets-your-vote-for-mighty-drive-to-p3-in-monaco.4OALiqRbQW3MCAP22BCw7Q.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Delighted Ocon 'on a cloud' as Alpine claim first podium since 2021 in Monaco|date=28 May 2023|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.delighted-ocon-on-a-cloud-as-alpine-claim-first-podium-since-2021-in-monaco.6YzMdBNx2FkwQg5MxStxmt.html|access-date=29 May 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=28 May 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528210636/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.delighted-ocon-on-a-cloud-as-alpine-claim-first-podium-since-2021-in-monaco.6YzMdBNx2FkwQg5MxStxmt.html|url-status=live}}</ref> More points came at the [[2023 Spanish Grand Prix|Spanish]] and [[2023 Canadian Grand Prix|Canadian]] Grands Prix and in the rain-affected {{F1 GP|2023|Austrian}} sprint race where he held off Ferrari's [[Charles Leclerc]] and McLaren's [[Lando Norris]]. In the main race, Ocon finished outside the points after receiving a penalty for an unsafe pit box release. Post race, he received another four penalties for track limits violations, totalling 30 seconds.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Verstappen makes it five wins in a row with Austria victory |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.verstappen-beats-leclerc-for-victory-in-austria-to-make-it-five-wins-in-a.40RQJjhwhd2nethv4qEsyJ.html |access-date=6 July 2023 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en |archive-date=3 July 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230703060619/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.verstappen-beats-leclerc-for-victory-in-austria-to-make-it-five-wins-in-a.40RQJjhwhd2nethv4qEsyJ.html |url-status=live }}</ref> His five penalties for the Grand Prix gave him the record for the most driving penalties in a single race in the history of Formula One.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://racingnews365.com/ocon-sets-dubious-f1-record-in-austria|title=Ocon sets dubious F1 record in Austria|website=racingnews365.com|first1=Michael|last1=Butterworth|first2=Aaron|last2=Deckers|date=3 July 2023|accessdate=3 July 2023|archive-date=3 July 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230703175317/https://racingnews365.com/ocon-sets-dubious-f1-record-in-austria|url-status=live}}</ref> Consecutive retirements followed with a hydraulics leak at the {{F1 GP|2023|British}} and a first-lap crash at the {{F1 GP|2023|Hungarian}}. He improved from fourteenth on the grid at the {{F1 GP|2023|Belgian}} to score points in eighth place.

Ocon retired from the {{F1 GP|2023|Italian}} "for safety reasons" due to a steering issue.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://racingnews365.com/ocon-explains-safety-issues-that-caused-monza-retirement|title=Ocon explains safety issues that caused Monza retirement|website=racingnews365.com|first1=Rory|last1=Mitchell|first2=Aaron|last2=Deckers|date=5 September 2023|accessdate=8 February 2024}}</ref> He then retired from sixth place at the {{F1 GP|2023|Singapore}} with a gearbox problem, his fourth non-finish in six races.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.not-the-best-birthday-says-race-retiree-ocon-as-gasly-comes-home-p6-after.7ix1yIuDsHM6o5mGOs02TX.html|title='Not the best birthday' says race retiree Ocon, as Gasly comes home P6 after 'intense' Singapore Grand Prix|website=formula1.com|date=18 September 2023|accessdate=8 February 2024}}</ref> He finished the {{F1 GP|2023|Qatar}} in seventh despite the hot weather conditions causing him to vomit into his helmet.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/1037757/1/ocon-was-throwing-cockpit-after-15-laps-due-intense-qatar-heat|title=Ocon was 'throwing up' in cockpit after 15 laps due to intense Qatar heat|website=crash.net|first=Lewis|last=Larkam|date=8 October 2023|accessdate=8 February 2024}}</ref> His seventh retirement of the season came at the {{F1 GP|2023|United States}} after a collision with [[Oscar Piastri]]. Ocon started sixteenth at the inaugural {{F1 GP|2023|Las Vegas}}, avoided collisions to improve to eighth on the first lap and climbed to fourth place by the end of the race. He ended the season twelfth in the World Drivers' Championship with 58 points, one place and four points behind teammate Gasly.

==== 2024: Early departure ====
[[File:Esteban Ocon 2024 Chinese GP.jpg|thumb|left|Ocon at the [[2024 Chinese Grand Prix]]]]
Ocon continued alongside Gasly at Alpine for {{F1|2024}}. During pre-season testing, he noted that the team were "on the back foot".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.alpine-drivers-admit-team-on-the-back-foot-heading-into-2024.3ZeFMgcILBn1aSGZ7Bi60C.html|title=Alpine drivers admit team 'on the back foot' heading into 2024|website=formula1.com|date=27 February 2024|accessdate=16 March 2024}}</ref> The Alpine drivers qualified nineteenth and twentieth for the season-opening {{F1 GP|2024|Bahrain}}, which Gasly described as "not a surprise".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.we-have-a-lot-of-work-ahead-of-us-alpine-drivers-say-double-q1-exit-not-a.5EFWYAdo9eZoruH8TDlaPA.html|title='We have a lot of work ahead of us' – Alpine drivers say double-Q1 exit 'not a surprise' in Bahrain|website=formula1.com|date=1 March 2024|accessdate=16 March 2024}}</ref> The Alpine did not reach the second qualifying session of a Grand Prix until Ocon did so at the third race, the {{F1 GP|2024|Australian}}; however, Ocon still finished sixteenth.

Ocon claimed the team's first points of 2024 at the {{F1 GP|2024|Miami}}, improving from thirteenth on the grid to tenth at the finish. He qualified eleventh at the {{F1 GP|2024|Monaco}} but retired after colliding with Gasly on track, for which he apologised and claimed responsibility.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/alpine-not-ruling-out-f1-driver-line-up-change-after-latest-ocon-gasly-clash/10616647/|title=Alpine not ruling out F1 driver line-up change after latest Ocon/Gasly clash|website=motorsport.com|first=Jonathan|last=Noble|date=27 May 2024|accessdate=28 May 2024}}</ref> A week later, Alpine announced Ocon would leave the team at the end of the season.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Barretto |first=Lawrence |date=3 June 2024 |title=Alpine to part ways with Ocon at end of 2024 season |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/breaking-alpine-announce-they-will-part-ways-with-ocon-at-end-of-2024-season.7ra4uaXdrYOHfklwU9TEqH |access-date=3 June 2024 |website=Formula1.com |publisher=[[Formula One Administration]] |language=en}}</ref> During the {{F1 GP|2024|Canadian}}, Alpine imposed [[team orders]] forcing Ocon to give up ninth to Gasly, who was in better position to attack Daniel Ricciardo. However, after Gasly failed to pass Ricciardo, Alpine did not ask Gasly to give the place back to Ocon, upsetting Ocon.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Ocon unhappy with Alpine team orders in Canada |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/ocon-unhappy-with-nonsense-team-orders-in-canada-despite-double-points.74r9MgUW4haFOumwFOZBb1 |access-date=4 November 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> Ocon scored points at the [[2024 Spanish Grand Prix|Spanish]] and [[2024 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgian]] Grands Prix.

Ocon did not score points for the next six races, but Alpine picked up a double podium (its first podium of the year) at the rain-affected [[2024 São Paulo Grand Prix|Sao Paulo Grand Prix]], with Ocon finishing second and Gasly third. Ocon led the race for a period but was overtaken by eventual winner Max Verstappen.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Alpine pair overjoyed by unexpected double podium in Brazil |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/we-never-gave-up-and-here-we-are-alpine-pair-overjoyed-by-unexpected-double.62mmKviVydA0WmbOHp1zpc |access-date=4 November 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

Ocon was replaced by [[Jack Doohan]] for the season-ending {{F1GP|2024|Abu Dhabi}}.<ref name="AD24">{{cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13264472/esteban-ocon-to-make-early-alpine-exit-as-jack-doohan-gets-to-start-f1-career-at-abu-dhabi-gp|title=Esteban Ocon to make early Alpine exit as Jack Doohan gets to start F1 career at Abu Dhabi GP|date=1 December 2024|access-date=1 December 2024}}</ref> Formula One's website reported that Alpine required Ocon to leave the team one race early in exchange for releasing him to [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] for the Abu Dhabi post-season test. In a message on Instagram, Ocon thanked the team and wrote that "this is not how I wanted things to end."<ref>{{Cite web |title=Ocon shares emotional farewell to Alpine |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/this-is-not-how-i-wanted-things-to-end-ocon-shares-emotional-farewell-to.XUOx2kM5WjY99EU8tdOdw |access-date=3 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

=== Haas (2025–present) ===
[[File:2025 Japan GP - Haas - Esteban Ocon - FP2.jpg|thumb|right|Ocon (pictured at the {{F1GP|2025|Japanese}}) signed for [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] in {{F1|2025}}.|alt=Ocon driving the Haas VF-25 at the 2025 Japanese Grand Prix]]
Ocon joined [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] on a multi-year deal from {{F1|2025}} onwards, partnering rookie [[Oliver Bearman]].<ref name="contract">{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cv2gzp0v0z7o |title=Haas sign Alpine's Ocon for 2025 season |date=25 July 2024 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=22 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240829182841/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cv2gzp0v0z7o |archive-date=29 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> After Haas struggled for performance at the season-opening {{F1GP|2025|Australian}},<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/inside-the-aero-problems-that-will-keep-haas-near-the-back-of-the-f1-field/10705192/ |title=Inside the aero problems that will keep Haas near the back of the F1 field |last1=Boxall-Legge
|first1=Jake |last2=Karpov |first2=Oleg |date=20 March 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 March 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250322221329/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/inside-the-aero-problems-that-will-keep-haas-near-the-back-of-the-f1-field/10705192/ |archive-date=22 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he finished fifth at the {{F1GP|2025|Chinese}} following disqualifications for both [[Scuderia Ferrari|Ferrari]] drivers, achieving his first points finish in the [[Haas VF-25|VF-25]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/leclerc-hamilton-and-gasly-disqualified-from-chinese-gp/10706422/ |title=Leclerc, Hamilton and Gasly disqualified from Chinese GP |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=23 March 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 March 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250323122436/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/leclerc-hamilton-and-gasly-disqualified-from-chinese-gp/10706422/ |archive-date=23 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished eighteenth in [[2025 Japanese Grand Prix|Japan]] on an alternate strategy.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://racer.com/2025/04/06/verstappen-cruises-to-fourth-straight-japanese-gp-win/ |title=Verstappen cruises to fourth straight Japanese GP win |last=Lamonato |first=Michael |date=6 April 2025 |magazine=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer]] |publisher=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer Media & Marketing Inc.]] |access-date=6 April 2025 |issn=1066-6060 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406180026/https://racer.com/2025/04/06/verstappen-cruises-to-fourth-straight-japanese-gp-win/ |archive-date=6 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After crashing out of qualifying and starting fourteenth in [[2025 Bahrain Grand Prix|Bahrain]], Ocon climbed to eighth on an alternate strategy.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://fr.motorsport.com/f1/news/8e-ocon-content-se-rattraper-apres-erreur-qualifications/10713126/ |title=Ocon "content" de s'être "rattrapé" après son crash en qualifications |trans-title=Ocon "content" with having "caught up" after his qualifying crash |last1=Courbon |first1=Téha |last2=Gaillard |first2=Fabien |date= |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=fr |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250415161918/https://fr.motorsport.com/f1/news/8e-ocon-content-se-rattraper-apres-erreur-qualifications/10713126/ |archive-date=15 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claimed fourteenth at the {{F1GP|2025|Saudi Arabian}}.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/f1/le-miracle-attendu-nest-pas-venu-pour-ocon-en-arabie-saoudite.html |title=Le miracle attendu n'est pas venu pour Ocon en Arabie saoudite |trans-title=The expected miracle did not come for Ocon in Saudi Arabia |last=Grangier |first=Dorian |date=21 April 2025 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=21 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250421214840/https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/f1/le-miracle-attendu-nest-pas-venu-pour-ocon-en-arabie-saoudite.html |archive-date=21 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

